                                                    Mobile App Active Session: Cart_Items: [Laptop, Phone]
                                                    Web Browser: Updating cart items...
                                                    Background Monitor Checked Data: Cart_Items: [Laptop, Phone], [Headphones]
                                                    
                                                    --- Final Database/Cache State ---
                                                    Production Cache Content: {USER_101=Cart_Items: [Laptop, Phone], [Headphones]}



MNC Level Code Decisions (Is PoC se kya seekha?)

1. No null Checking Hassle (getOrDefault):
MNCs mein agar direct map.get(key) likhoge aur key absent hui, toh code null dega jo aage chalke NullPointerException (NPE) ban sakta hai. 
Production code mein hum getOrDefault(key, defaultValue) use karte hain taaki null ka kissa hi khatam ho jaye.
2. Atomic APIs over conditional blocks:
Real world mein if(!map.containsKey(key)) { map.put(key, value); } likhna sakht mana hota hai kyunki yeh thread-safe nahi hai (race condition banata hai).
Iski jagah Java 8 ke modern atomic methods jaise computeIfAbsent(), putIfAbsent(), aur computeIfPresent() ka use kiya jata hai, 
jo internally buckets ko lock karke smoothly kaam karte hain.

